    "content": [
      "Many of us find managing up to be anxiety-inducing. I can't say I've mastered it, but here's a framework for what I strive to do every day / week: inform, align, anticipate.",
      "Informing is about ensuring my manager is aware of how I'm managing my time and energy. My objective is to ensure my manager is never caught off-guard by something I'm involved in. This is helpful for both of us: my manager has information to work with, and I get early signals of misalignment.",
      "Aligning is the more overt work of ensuring we're singing from the same song sheet before I go too far down a path. My manager has context that I lack, and when I seek alignment, I'm checking my blind spots. If we're misaligned on my / our work, it's better to find out as early as possible before things diverge past the point of no return.",
      "Anticipating is almost the result of effective informing and aligning. By doing the work of the former, I'm able to anticipate what my manager needs and with any luck, be an effective thought partner. This is my ultimate goal with managing up: to be more than simply the next rung below. I want to be the belay line.",
      "What do you think? What have I missed? How do you manage up?"
    ]
